I need to implement word_count. Approach: lowercase, then split on characters that are neither alphanumeric nor apostrophe. Then strip leading/trailing apostrophes from each token. Skip empty tokens.

Note that the tests have `#[ignore]` on most of them. The instructions say "so that the tests pass" — probably run with --ignored. I'll implement it and run with --include-ignored.

Implementation:

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

pub fn word_count(words: &str) -> HashMap<String, u32> {
    let mut counts = HashMap::new();
    for token in words.to_lowercase().split(|c: char| !c.is_alphanumeric() && c != '\'') {
        let word = token.trim_matches('\'');
        if word.is_empty() {
            continue;
        }
        *counts.entry(word.to_string()).or_insert(0) += 1;
    }
    counts
}
```

